# Copy this to .env.docker and fill in the AI provider keys, then:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.docker up --build
#
# This brings up CADAM plus a full local Supabase backend (Postgres, Auth,
# PostgREST, Realtime, Storage) — no `supabase start` / Supabase CLI needed.
# See README.md's "Docker" section for the full walkthrough.

############
